    affiliation: "Leiden Institute of Chemistry, Leiden University"

version: "0.8.3"
url: "https://github.com/rskort/LiNaK/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rskort/LiNaK/"
license: "Apache-2.0"

abstract: >
  LiNaK is a Python package for molecular dynamics trajectory analysis,
  visualization, and workflow-oriented data handling. It provides command-line
  and Python interfaces for computing and plotting density profiles,
  mean-squared displacement, atom-resolved positions, radial distribution
  functions, coordination metrics, electrostatic-potential-related quantities,
  and water orientation analyses. LiNaK is designed with particular emphasis on
  electrochemical and interfacial simulation workflows, while remaining
  applicable to general molecular dynamics trajectories. The package supports
  HDF5-based data storage and reproducible metadata-rich outputs, and includes
  utilities for common CP2K and LAMMPS workflows.

keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - trajectory analysis
  - electrochemistry
  - interfacial systems
  - electrode-electrolyte interfaces
  - HDF5
  - data visualization
  - CP2K
  - LAMMPS
  - radial distribution function
  - mean-squared displacement
  - water orientation